A leap year contains 366 days due to the addition of February 29. Given a year, task is to check if it's is a leap year or not. For example, 2024 is a leap year, whereas 2026 is a common year.

Approach
Check divisibility by 4: First verify whether the given year is divisible by 4, because most leap years follow this rule.
Exclude century years divisible by 100: If the year is divisible by 100, it is usually not a leap year, so this condition must be checked to avoid incorrect results.
Allow years divisible by 400: If a year is divisible by 400, it is considered a leap year even though it is also divisible by 100.
Apply conditions using if-elif-else: Combine these rules in conditional statements so the program can correctly determine whether the year is a leap year or not.
Code Implementation

year = int(input("Enter a year:"))

if year % 4 == 0 and year % 100 != 0: 
    print(year, "is a leap year")
elif year % 400 == 0:
    print(year, "is a leap year")
else:
    print(year, "is not a leap year")
Output

Enter a year:2024
2024 is a leap year

Explanation:

It first takes the year as input using input() and converts it to an integer using int() so arithmetic operations can be performed.
year % 4 == 0 checks whether the year is divisible by 4, which is the basic requirement for a leap year.
year % 100 != 0 ensures that years divisible by 100 are not treated as leap years.
year % 400 == 0 handles the special case where a century year divisible by 400 is still considered a leap year.
These conditions are combined using if-elif-else statements to determine and print whether the given year is a leap year or not.
